INTRO={'title':'How federal information-security policy developed','deck':'The history of OMB Circular A-130, the laws that shaped it, and the technical standards agencies use to protect information.','chronology':'Compare laws, OMB policies, and technical publications over time. Select an event to read about the document and open its sources.','revisions':'Six major editions show how A-130 changed as federal computing, public services, and security responsibilities developed.','authority':'Responsibility varies by subject. A-130 provides much of the management framework, while laws and presidential directives also assign work directly to NIST and other agencies.','library':'Find a document by title, subject, or phrase. Use the filters to narrow the list by date, document type, or relationship to A-130.'}
AUTHORITY_CLOSE=paragraphs('A NIST publication becomes a requirement for a particular use through the authority that adopts it. That may be a federal standard, an OMB policy, a regulation, or a contract. Agency officials remain responsible for carrying out the duties assigned to them by law and policy. This is why the technical standard and the agency instruction often need to be read together.')

# Place each quotation beside the paragraph it illustrates.
for _id,_title,_body,_refs in SUMMARIES:
 if _body[-1]['kind']=='quote':
  _position={'a130-1985':1,'a130-1996':3,'a130-2016':2}[_id]
  _body.insert(_position,_body.pop())
RELATION_LABELS={'Chronological association':'Related development','Explicit OMB direction':'Directed by OMB','Explicit statutory mandate':'Assigned by law','Implementation support':'Guidance for implementation','Later incorporation':'Later adopted in policy','Separate executive direction':'Directed by the President'}
